e\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. If you need to perform multiple actions, you can always send more messages with additional tool calls. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Pre-launch dry run of the onboarding harness from a clean session — prove fld-4471's flow stands up from zero: confirm it's in our roster, pull its live telemetry, then try the imagery manifest. Give me the field's real telemetry readings plus exactly what the manifest call comes back with.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `manifest_error`, `manifest_hint`, `telemetry_reading_ref`, `telemetry_ndvi`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value — ONE value per field (a single scalar; if your work touched several items, report only the final/target value for each field, never a list or per-item map)."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"gAAAAABqQ05JDcmDHldl1mOtD4du4TEu7cQ9_JpJywIJxBB8Z1sCMnxHhkMRlZMHPdL318hceh7_sblOOTNBZBCOHWfrAcVyS-IfBGr9YbRCkQWw5-j8IPED_QJz7jX_peqBAt0cNQU4lvU1RJpadX-ztdJSQvJ4EmSMnL67E91H4I5x9j9mUjl15QUTn0O5dNq_fCLyZds8U_hETlxJCLmhnBBMZVjbl642GTNwwX7aQK-E-OObjRnUge9usSl0RiORmfI5taDX1cKVXvIIl8WNcHPgUarVUD6unETmmwPgijOu3QYtYn0dkgZnL7t8c7GcOG_xhjPd3W8qWt_OsDm6eiSjJQ12BliqBGgS5FXh6y9YvGXu7zF8XfOAvmcGCUmwHbq66M2sV-Su2Mcuqa3KuoM8thQc8_l9dijO2IEmDo6vyH8zlz1g7BzOD_gN5GNG1e5Eqpc_vzyhTODUw07LsF-e2tskMXAJpSn1BHcDvYfset2O9hMigHWEoiPqNgFmBbIk9-LAGE_nthSgdQKQMI27dbokyoUA1cnxOB